In article <33D9CC16.28A2@ioc.ee>, Marko Vendelin  <markov@ioc.ee> wrote:
>2. Hardware compatibility issues: Are the memory chips in Alphas
>the        same as in PPros? Are PC monitors from compatible with
>Alphas?

The UDB and "alpha PC motherboards" use 36 bits ECC SIMM memory modules ;
most PCs use 32 bits ones, but some use the same modules. My UDB runs
with 24 MB from DEC and 16 MB I found on a PC 486.

The UDB use a standard (S)VGA monitor. As Alpha PCs use standard PCI video
cards, they also use the same monitors as PCs.

I believe the hardware is most compatible between the two systems. However,
cache memory is likely not to be the same model. Also, some PCI cards might
not be supported, if the PC bios of these cards try fancy things that are
not well handled by the PC emulator in the Alpha ROM.

	--Thomas Pornin



