Nope! You could get the IDE Version, which is around 3.5kMark
cheaper. It's got an Elsa Winner2000AVI/3D graphics card which
IS supported by the S3V X-Server in XFree-3.3. As far as I know,
the Diamond Fire is NOT supported (or has this changed in the mean-
time? Anyone?). The machine is a PC164 w/21164@500MHz with 64megs
RAM, 3.8GB WD Caviar IDE disk and a Samsung 8X IDE CD-ROM plus a
cheap sound card.

Buy the Adaptec yourself, I got the 2940UW and it's working fine
now. Things are cheaper this way, you may even think about NOT
buying a 12X SCSI CD-ROM. 8X on IDE seems good enough (from my point
of view).

Concerning the three years warranty: Forget it. They sell the system
with WNT installed. If you change things, like installing Linux, the
warranty is VOID. You'd have to reinstall WNT BEFORE they help you.

There are more alternatives: I feel the people at VOBIS, a large
german retailer, don't really know all too much about the Alpha.
Better stick with the pros. Find out who's willing to make a good
deal by contacting the retailers who help you with hard- and software
problems on RedHat's axp-list. They give you a three years warranty
WITH Linux preinstalled.

So you better check the mailing list to see what's good for you!

