Heikki Virkkunen <tesno@pato.vaala.fi> wrote:
>Someone then told me that i need at least 2.1.24 kernel to start netscape
>with news libs. I just fetched it, and when I tried to apply axp-diffs-2.1.1
>from azstarnet, i received an error:

axp-diffs-2.1.1 is a patch against the 2.1.1 kernel, not the 2.1.24. The
2.1.x series evolve at high speed, so this incompatibility is not surprising.

Anyway, no axp-diffs-2.1.24 exists, for the good reason that it was not needed
anymore. The recent 2.1.x kernels include all the features the axp-diffs
used to add to 2.0.x kernels. So just grab the stock kernel sources and
forget axp-diff.

If you want a 2.1.x kernel reasonably stable, use the 2.1.36 or 2.1.42.
Avoid the very latest (2.1.44 and 2.1.45) as they did some evil things on
filesystems (this code is actually completely rewritten).

	--Thomas Pornin



