Q: How do I get my serial port/modem combo to work at speeds greater than 
38.4K?

A: You need to use the "setserial" program to configure your serial port
connected to your modem to talk at a higher speed. Add the line

                      setserial /dev/modem spd_vhi 

to your /etc/rc.d/rc.serial file.  RedHat doesn't install this file, so
just create it in rc.d. There are reports that Seyon still doesn't behave
properly but that minicom and dip do. 
------------

