prices only for the NT models.  They seem to be giving an extra economic
_dis_incentive to using THEIR OWN product!  The pricing structure looks
designed to kill of DEC Unix (which DEC makes money from) and giving its
market to NT (which you-know-who makes money from).  As I see it, DEC has
been, for lack of a better term, "assimilated."  They have turned into 
JANTR (Just Another NT Reseller).
</soapbox>

-Chris



