Hi!

Here's what I found out about installing the Tcl/Tk extension BLT-2.1-1.
I couldn't get the thing to build a binary rpm from the source rpm.

As always, read the instructions on the label first, the .spec file.
You can learn from it that the source rpm was designed to work in
conjunction with itcl-2.2.

To build itcl-2.2, all you have to do is add 'alpha' to the
ExclusiveArch line in the spec file, then it builds fine.
Now BLT-2.1-1.src.rpm can be built.

Hope this post helps to keep useless requests like my original one off
the list...

