1. I recommend you go with Micron 50ns 32mb 72pin SIMMs.
(For overclocking performance freaks this brand has the best
reputation.)

2. I'm not sure that the ATI is well supported for the ALPHA.
(Most people tend to use the #9 Imagine 128-2 or the Matrox Millenium.)

3. You will probably want to upgrade to a 300-400watt power supply.
(Alpha CPUs draw some serious current!)

4. There is a US company which sells 500mhz Alpha systems for
less the US$3000 referenced in US Computer Shopper.

5. The version of the MB which supports OSF/1 costs a premium compared
to the Windoze NT version of the board (which also runs Linux).

6. While flying a computer from the US may seem extreme I believe that
most of the pieces discussed will either originate or be routed though
the US in any case.  So it's just a matter of what stage in the game.


