peterm@landau.EECS.Berkeley.EDU (Peter Mardahl) writes:

>   Some months ago I heard of some memory/kernel problems
> on PC164 boards, which cropped up during heavy use.

There's a paging problem on PC164 boards which only appears when you
have 128 or 256 megs of ram. The fix is the new MILO image at
gatekeeper, or:

MILO> set MEMORY_SIZE 120 (for 128 megs, or 252 for 256)

However, this problem appears quite quickly, so maybe it isn't what
you were thinking about.

-- g




